+# U-Boot environment location on the JL12D2 / MCL12D2 (OEM LX510 U-Boot).
+#
+# Deliberately a FILE, not flash -- the same fix as the MC-A85. This OEM U-Boot
+# keeps its saveenv copy at flash 0x30000, the first block of the kernel
+# partition (mtd1), and thingino's default "/dev/mtd1 0x0" pointed straight at
+# it: S97sysupgrade's "mark sysupgrade complete" on the first boot after a
+# flash wrote an env block over the uImage header, and the next power-on found
+# no kernel. U-Boot boots from its built-in bootargs, so nothing needs to reach
+# its env from Linux; fw_setenv/fw_printenv work against this scratch file.
+#
+# <device> <offset> <env size>
+/etc/fw_env.dat 0x0 0x10000
